1
00:07:49,411 --> 00:07:55,411
William Tell is a action, adventure, drama film directed by Nick Hamm.

2
00:15:38,823 --> 00:15:44,823
The narrative unfolds in the 14th Century, when the European
nations vie for supremacy within the Holy Roman Empire.

3
00:23:28,235 --> 00:23:34,235
The ambitious Austrian Empire, desiring more land, invades
neighbouring Switzerland, a serene and pastoral nation.

4
00:31:17,647 --> 00:31:23,647
Protagonist William Tell, a formerly peaceful hunter, finds himself forced to take action as his family
and homeland come under threat from the oppressive Austrian King and his ruthless warlords.

5
00:39:07,058 --> 00:39:13,058
William Tell, played by Claes Bang.

6
00:46:56,470 --> 00:47:02,470
Gessler, played by Connor Swindells.

7
00:54:45,882 --> 00:54:51,882
Suna, played by Golshifteh Farahani.

8
01:02:35,294 --> 01:02:41,294
Rudenz, played by Jonah Hauer-King.

9
01:10:24,705 --> 01:10:30,705
Princess Bertha, played by Ellie Bamber.

10
01:18:14,117 --> 01:18:20,117
Stauffacher, played by Rafe Spall.

11
01:26:03,529 --> 01:26:09,529
William Tell is a 2024 epic historical action film written and directed by Nick
Hamm, based on the play of the same name by Friedrich Schiller.

12
01:33:52,941 --> 01:33:58,941
It stars Claes Bang as the titular character, as well as Connor Swindells, Golshifteh Farahani, Jonah
Hauer-King, Tobias Jowett, Ellie Bamber, Rafe Spall, Emily Beecham, Jonathan Pryce, and Ben Kingsley.

13
01:41:42,352 --> 01:41:48,352
The film had its world premiere at the Toronto International Film Festival on 5 September
2024, and was theatrically released in the United Kingdom on 10 January 2025.

14
01:49:31,764 --> 01:49:37,764
It received mixed reviews.

15
01:57:21,176 --> 01:57:27,176
The film explores themes of switzerland, rape and murder,
apple, middle ages (476-1453), medieval.

16
02:05:10,588 --> 02:05:16,588
The tone is emotional.
